W - Fork Axiom

To fork is to see two truths at once. The Diagonal / Fork Axiom duplicates the second argument for the first, creating internal feedback.
W f x = f x x.

🌊

@[ts]

// 🔗 Implicit Gravity: No imports required. Dependencies are in the DNA.
export const W = <A, B>(f: (x: A) => (y: A) => B) => (x: A): B => f(x)(x);


@[rs]

// 🔗 Native implementation
pub fn W<A, B, F>(f: F, x: A) -> B
where
    F: Fn(A) -> Box<dyn Fn(A) -> B>,
    A: Clone,
{
    f(x.clone())(x)
}


